---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const lessons = [
  {
    number: 1,
    title: "Hello, C64!",
    description: "Your first PRINT command and seeing results on screen",
    status: "available"
  },
  {
    number: 2,
    title: "Screen Control with CHR$()",
    description: "Clear the screen, move the cursor, and control output",
    status: "available"
  },
  {
    number: 3,
    title: "Line Numbers and GOTO",
    description: "Create programs that loop and repeat",
    status: "available"
  },
  {
    number: 4,
    title: "Border Colours with POKE",
    description: "Change colours by writing directly to memory",
    status: "available"
  },
  {
    number: 5,
    title: "Variables: Storing Information",
    description: "Remember numbers and text using variables",
    status: "available"
  },
  {
    number: 6,
    title: "Reading the Keyboard with GET",
    description: "Make programs interactive with keyboard input",
    status: "available"
  },
  {
    number: 7,
    title: "Making Decisions with IF/THEN",
    description: "Programs that branch based on conditions",
    status: "available"
  },
  {
    number: 8,
    title: "Your First Complete Game",
    description: "Combine everything to build Number Hunter",
    status: "available"
  }
];
---

<Layout title="Week 1: BASIC Fundamentals - Commodore 64">
  <style>
    .course-hero {
      background: linear-gradient(135deg, #4a4dff 0%, #7c70da 100%);
      color: white;
      padding: var(--space-12) var(--space-4);
      text-align: center;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-12);
    }

    .course-title {
      font-family: var(--font-family-mono);
      font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3rem);
      font-weight: 900;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
      text-shadow: 2px 2px 4px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.3);
    }

    .course-subtitle {
      font-size: 1.25rem;
      opacity: 0.95;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
    }

    .course-description {
      max-width: 700px;
      margin: 0 auto var(--space-8);
      font-size: 1.125rem;
      line-height: 1.7;
      opacity: 0.95;
    }

    .course-stats {
      display: flex;
      gap: var(--space-8);
      justify-content: center;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
    }

    .stat-item {
      text-align: center;
    }

    .stat-value {
      font-size: 2rem;
      font-weight: bold;
      font-family: var(--font-family-mono);
    }

    .stat-label {
      font-size: 0.875rem;
      opacity: 0.9;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    }

    .content-container {
      max-width: 1000px;
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 0 var(--space-4);
    }

    .section-title {
      font-size: 2rem;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
      color: var(--color-text);
    }

    .intro-section {
      background: var(--color-surface);
      border: 2px solid #4a4dff;
      border-radius: 0.75rem;
      padding: var(--space-8);
      margin-bottom: var(--space-12);
    }

    .intro-section h2 {
      color: #4a4dff;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
      font-size: 1.5rem;
    }

    .intro-section p {
      color: var(--color-text-secondary);
      line-height: 1.7;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
    }

    .intro-section ul {
      color: var(--color-text-secondary);
      line-height: 1.7;
      padding-left: var(--space-6);
    }

    .intro-section li {
      margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
    }

    .lessons-grid {
      display: grid;
      gap: var(--space-4);
      margin-bottom: var(--space-12);
    }

    .lesson-card {
      background: var(--color-surface);
      border: 2px solid var(--color-border);
      border-radius: 0.75rem;
      padding: var(--space-6);
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: auto 1fr auto;
      gap: var(--space-4);
      align-items: center;
      text-decoration: none;
      color: var(--color-text);
      transition: all var(--transition-base);
    }

    .lesson-card:hover {
      border-color: #4a4dff;
      transform: translateX(4px);
      box-shadow: 0 4px 12px rgba(74, 77, 255, 0.1);
    }

    .lesson-number {
      width: 50px;
      height: 50px;
      background: linear-gradient(135deg, #4a4dff 0%, #7c70da 100%);
      color: white;
      border-radius: 50%;
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: center;
      font-family: var(--font-family-mono);
      font-size: 1.25rem;
      font-weight: bold;
    }

    .lesson-content {
      flex: 1;
    }

    .lesson-title {
      font-size: 1.25rem;
      font-weight: 600;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-1);
      color: var(--color-text);
    }

    .lesson-description {
      color: var(--color-text-secondary);
      font-size: 0.9rem;
      line-height: 1.5;
    }

    .lesson-status {
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: var(--space-2);
      font-size: 0.875rem;
      font-weight: 500;
      padding: var(--space-2) var(--space-3);
      border-radius: 9999px;
      background: rgba(74, 77, 255, 0.1);
      color: #4a4dff;
    }

    .start-button {
      display: inline-block;
      padding: var(--space-4) var(--space-8);
      background: linear-gradient(135deg, #4a4dff 0%, #7c70da 100%);
      color: white;
      font-size: 1.125rem;
      font-weight: 600;
      text-decoration: none;
      border-radius: 0.5rem;
      transition: all var(--transition-base);
    }

    .start-button:hover {
      transform: translateY(-2px);
      box-shadow: 0 8px 20px rgba(74, 77, 255, 0.3);
    }

    .wow-box {
      background: var(--color-bg);
      border-left: 4px solid #4a4dff;
      padding: var(--space-4);
      margin: var(--space-6) 0;
      border-radius: 0 0.5rem 0.5rem 0;
    }

    .wow-box strong {
      color: #4a4dff;
      font-family: var(--font-family-mono);
    }

    @media (max-width: 768px) {
      .lesson-card {
        grid-template-columns: 1fr;
        text-align: center;
      }

      .lesson-number {
        margin: 0 auto;
      }

      .lesson-status {
        justify-self: center;
      }
    }
  </style>

  <!-- Course Hero -->
  <section class="course-hero">
    <h1 class="course-title">WEEK 1: BASIC FUNDAMENTALS</h1>
    <p class="course-subtitle">Start Programming the Commodore 64</p>

    <p class="course-description">
      Over 8 lessons, you'll learn the fundamentals of C64 BASIC programming.
      From your first PRINT command to building a complete interactive game,
      you'll develop real programming skills while creating programs that actually do something.
      No prior experience required—just curiosity and willingness to experiment!
    </p>

    <div class="course-stats">
      <div class="stat-item">
        <div class="stat-value">8</div>
        <div class="stat-label">Lessons</div>
      </div>
      <div class="stat-item">
        <div class="stat-value">10-15</div>
        <div class="stat-label">Minutes Each</div>
      </div>
      <div class="stat-item">
        <div class="stat-value">1</div>
        <div class="stat-label">Complete Game</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Course Introduction -->
  <div class="content-container">
    <section class="intro-section">
      <h2>What You'll Learn This Week</h2>

      <p>
        Week 1 covers the essential building blocks of programming. By the end of these 8 lessons,
        you'll understand how to:
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li><strong>Display output</strong> with PRINT and screen control commands</li>
        <li><strong>Create programs</strong> using line numbers and loops</li>
        <li><strong>Control hardware</strong> directly with POKE (colours, memory)</li>
        <li><strong>Store data</strong> in variables (numbers and text)</li>
        <li><strong>Read input</strong> from the keyboard with GET</li>
        <li><strong>Make decisions</strong> using IF/THEN conditional logic</li>
        <li><strong>Build complete programs</strong> that combine all these skills</li>
      </ul>

      <div class="wow-box">
        <strong>Week 1 Goal:</strong> By Lesson 8, you'll have created "Number Hunter"—a fully playable
        guessing game with scoring, lives, colour feedback, and replay functionality. This demonstrates
        that you're not just learning—you're actually programming.
      </div>

      <p>
        <strong>Prerequisites:</strong> None! These lessons assume zero prior programming experience.
        You'll need access to a Commodore 64 (real hardware or emulator like VICE) and the patience
        to type in programs and experiment.
      </p>

      <p>
        <strong>Learning approach:</strong> Each lesson is 10-15 minutes of focused learning.
        Every lesson ends with a "wow moment"—something that makes you think "look what I can make this thing do!"
        The best way to learn is by doing, so type in the examples, try the experiments, and make mistakes.
        The C64 is remarkably forgiving—the worst that happens is you turn it off and on again!
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Lessons List -->
    <section>
      <h2 class="section-title">Lessons</h2>

      <div class="lessons-grid">
        {lessons.map(lesson => (
          <a href={`/commodore-64/basic/week-1/lesson-${String(lesson.number).padStart(2, '0')}`}
             class="lesson-card">
            <div class="lesson-number">{lesson.number}</div>
            <div class="lesson-content">
              <h3 class="lesson-title">{lesson.title}</h3>
              <p class="lesson-description">{lesson.description}</p>
            </div>
            <div class="lesson-status">Start →</div>
          </a>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Call to Action -->
    <section style="text-align: center; margin: var(--space-16) 0;">
      <h2 class="section-title">Ready to Start?</h2>
      <p style="color: var(--color-text-secondary); margin-bottom: var(--space-4); max-width: 600px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;">
        Turn on your C64 (or boot your emulator), wait for the "READY." prompt,
        and let's write your first line of code. The journey of a thousand programs
        begins with a single PRINT statement!
      </p>
      <a href="/commodore-64/basic/week-1/lesson-01" class="start-button">
        Start Lesson 1: Hello, C64!
      </a>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>